WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.560
A father and son facing off for control&nbsp;
of the family legacy. A damaged daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.040
willing to destroy a brother for her&nbsp;
father's sake. Where are Yellowstone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.789
Shakespearean-scale characters headed in Season 5?

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.360
Opening the season with a two-hour event,&nbsp;
Yellowstone Season 5 is set to premiere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.640
on November 15, 2022. Paramount has been on a&nbsp;
roll lately with Yellowstone-adjacent content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.060
as the network has greenlit multiple&nbsp;
Taylor Sheridan-helmed spinoff series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:30.360
including 1883, 1923, and 6666 proving&nbsp;
that they're all in on Yellowstone.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.320
Recently, series executive producer&nbsp;
David C. Glasser caught up with Hello!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.540
magazine to promote the next season, saying that,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.920
"Episode one will immediately surprise everybody&nbsp;
– where our story starts and what has happened."

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.400
It sounds like he's implying a series&nbsp;
time jump in the Yellowstone narrative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.120
or some other major event to kick off&nbsp;
the next season. While we're hard pressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.600
to figure out how you could start a new&nbsp;
season with more intensity than Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.440
there's no doubt that Sheridan and company&nbsp;
will deliver — and it will be explosive.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.760
The next installment of the Dutton family&nbsp;
saga arrives just in time for Thanksgiving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.220
something to make fans genuinely thankful.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.960
The central cast members of Yellowstone&nbsp;
are expected to return for Season 5. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.920
includes Kevin Costner as Dutton family&nbsp;
patriarch John, Kelly Reilly as Beth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.200
Cole Hauser as Rip, Wes Bentley as Jamie,&nbsp;
Luke Grimes as Kayce, and Kelsey Asbille&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.460
as Monica. Not to mention Jefferson White as&nbsp;
Jimmy and a host of others from the bunkhouse.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.600
When Season 4 ended, Kayce was immersed&nbsp;
in a Native American ritual that cut him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.480
off from the world, only to have&nbsp;
a spiritual revelation of his own.

00:01:27.793 --> 00:01:29.653
"I saw the end of us."

00:01:29.653 --> 00:01:32.880
There's plenty of speculation as&nbsp;
to what Kayce meant. With luck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.680
we'll learn the answer in the season premiere.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.340
The fifth season is guaranteed to bring a&nbsp;
new sheriff to town following the death of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.660
Donnie Haskell, played by Hugh Dillon. It's&nbsp;
possible that an existing character will step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.460
into the role. Matthew Jones, introduced as the&nbsp;
sheriff's deputy in Season 4, is a possibility.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.440
Sadly, Will Patton, who played Jamie's biological&nbsp;
father Garrett Randle, won't be returning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.280
since Jamie killed him in the Season 4&nbsp;
finale. However, Katherine Cunningham,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.880
who plays Christina, is likely to return&nbsp;
since she and Jamie have a child together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.060
How will that play out now that Beth has Jamie&nbsp;
under her thumb? We'll have to wait and see!

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.840
It's unclear what the central storyline of Season

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.980
5 will be. During a HALL Wines Happy&nbsp;
Hour interview, Cole Hauser hinted,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.580
"The way Season 4 ends, the audience ... will&nbsp;
be happily surprised with a lot of things."

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.080
"Who presents the bride?"

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.587
"Me. I'm her father."

00:02:20.587 --> 00:02:24.120
Between the marriage of Rip and Beth,&nbsp;
Kayce's revelation, and the "understanding"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.260
between Beth and Jamie, the next season of&nbsp;
Yellowstone promises to cover new territory.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.460
The biggest question heading into Season 5&nbsp;
concerns the race for governor, which has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.500
John and Jamie pitted against each other. John now&nbsp;
"owns" Jamie and is threatening his job prospects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.880
leaving plenty of fans to feel sorry for the&nbsp;
way Jamie has been treated. Perhaps John will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.420
reassess their relationship after notifying&nbsp;
the sheriff's daughter that her father is dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.480
and recognizing that Beth could&nbsp;
easily have killed his adopted son.

00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:50.822
"Did I lose a son today?"

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.120
"He was never your son, Daddy."

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.280
Hopefully, John and Jamie will reconcile.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.960
Kayce's arc will also be a crucial part&nbsp;
of Season 5. His decision to undergo the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.980
warrior initiation rite is sure to earn&nbsp;
the respect of Monica's family. It will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.820
undoubtedly affect his view of the world.&nbsp;
There's been speculation that Kayce may cross&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.780
over to the side of the Broken Rock Indian&nbsp;
Reservation. That would destroy his father.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.300
So far, every season of Yellowstone — excluding&nbsp;
the first with its 90-minute series premiere — has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.620
featured 10 one-hour episodes. Next season,&nbsp;
however, will be split into two halves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.720
with 7 episodes each. The longer 14-episode&nbsp;
fifth season is good news for patient fans.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.840
"You want me to drive?" "I drive."

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.920
The fifth season is expected to help launch&nbsp;
several new shows for Paramount's in-house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:40.680
streamer Paramount+, beyond Taylor Sheridan's two&nbsp;
sophomore series, 1883 and Mayor of Kingstown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:46.260
Among these are the Prohibition-era 1923 and&nbsp;
the Sylvester Stallone-led Tulsa King. Whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.740
these shows will connect to the greater&nbsp;
Yellowstone story has yet to be revealed.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.780
With an extended fifth season, and a 10.4 million&nbsp;
viewership average on the Paramount Network,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.920
Yellowstone shows no signs of slowing&nbsp;
down. By far the most profitable and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.400
beloved show on the network, Yellowstone&nbsp;
and its prequels and spinoffs are high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.690
priorities for the network, meaning&nbsp;
we'll likely see more in the future.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:11.280
In May 2022, Paramount announced that production&nbsp;
on Season 5 of Yellowstone had begun in Montana.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.200
Though the series is largely set in Paradise&nbsp;
Valley and Bozeman, it hasn't always filmed there.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.100
When Yellowstone premiered, the series&nbsp;
was primarily filmed in Park City, Utah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.420
southeast of Salt Lake City. The series&nbsp;
traveled all across the Beehive State&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.960
to capture the picturesque Western&nbsp;
landscape. However, since day one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.520
the Chief Joseph Ranch in Darby, Montana has&nbsp;
served as the infamous Yellowstone-Dutton Ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.720
and most likely will until the series&nbsp;
comes to a close. A family-owned ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.860
the Chief Joseph was well-known throughout&nbsp;
Montana long before TV came calling.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.760
After the third season, Yellowstone moved&nbsp;
production from Utah to the film-friendly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.080
state of Montana, hoping to honestly brand&nbsp;
the show as a "Made in Montana" production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.300
Season 5 continued the tradition, filming in and&nbsp;
around the Missoula area in the western part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.500
the state. The story takes place primarily in&nbsp;
Gallatin and Park Counties, but Yellowstone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.460
rarely films there, opting instead to keep&nbsp;
production to the western end of the state.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.540
While there is no official trailer&nbsp;
for Season 5 of Yellowstone just yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.000
there is a new 15 second teaser that claims that:

00:05:13.636 --> 00:05:18.300
"All will be revealed?" Tell us more. What&nbsp;
needs revealing? The election results:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.983
John or Jamie? Kayce's new&nbsp;
vision quest-enhanced world view?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.700
"What do you see?"

00:05:26.899 --> 00:05:28.379
"Two paths."

00:05:28.379 --> 00:05:30.180
Or is it something else entirely?

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:35.220
From what we can see in the teaser, which isn't&nbsp;
much, Kayce seems distraught. He puts his head in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:39.300
his hands as he sinks onto his front porch.&nbsp;
Could this be the start of conflict between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.140
Kayce and Monica? Or, more likely, between&nbsp;
his family and the rest of the Duttons?

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.360
Next we see Rip saddle up with a scoped rifle.&nbsp;
There's real trouble brewing. Whether it's human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.400
or animal-related is up for debate, but one thing&nbsp;
is clear: Rip aims to teach someone a lesson.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.400
"If you need something taken care of,&nbsp;
you tell me, and I'll take care of it."

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.400
The final teased moment shows John&nbsp;
Dutton walking down a hallway looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:03.660
all respectable. No doubt this involves his&nbsp;
gubernatorial campaign. He's most likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:09.120
on his way to give a speech but what kind?&nbsp;
Victory or concession? All will be revealed…

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:13.500
If you've never watched a single episode but&nbsp;
want to catch up or you want to revisit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.120
series' best moments before the season premiere,&nbsp;
Yellowstone is available to stream. Currently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.120
all four seasons can be found on&nbsp;
Peacock with the premium option.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.780
If Season 4 taught us anything, it's&nbsp;
that paying attention to small details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.260
in earlier seasons will be rewarded.&nbsp;
Kayce's vision of his dead brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.660
Lee, came as a surprise at&nbsp;
the end of the last season.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.560
Attentive fans remember that the eldest&nbsp;
Dutton son was killed in battle in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.640
series' opening episode. Sheridan's playing&nbsp;
the storytelling long game. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.420
those who have no interest in bingeing the&nbsp;
first four seasons can find recaps on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.060
Yellowstone YouTube page, all in under 20 minutes.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.620
If you're curious about some of the characters&nbsp;
from the Season 4 flashbacks, or if you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:54.240
interested in the Yellowstone universe beyond&nbsp;
the flagship show, the prequel series 1883 can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:59.160
be streamed in its entirety on Paramount+. The&nbsp;
Yellowstone origin story follows the Dutton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:03.300
family from Fort Worth, Texas across the great&nbsp;
plains as they journey to what would eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.920
be known as Paradise Valley, Montana. If you&nbsp;
love classic westerns, then this one's for you.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.280
Since its premiere in 2018, Yellowstone has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.220
taken the country — and especially&nbsp;
the Paramount Network — by storm.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:23.665
"I feel different here. My skin&nbsp;
tingles. Never felt like this before."

00:07:23.665 --> 00:07:27.180
Because of its high production values,&nbsp;
stellar cast, and raging popularity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.780
the Paramount Network runs frequent&nbsp;
Yellowstone marathons. No doubt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.820
they'll run another ahead&nbsp;
of the Season 5 premiere.

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:37.680
Marathons increase interest and excitement leading&nbsp;
up to the return of a popular program, and some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.820
of the greatest TV shows in history have done the&nbsp;
same in preparation for a new season — especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.000
if it can secure more consistent viewership&nbsp;
for their networks going forward.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.540
For those interested in bingeing&nbsp;
all of Yellowstone with commercials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:52.320
simply search online for information&nbsp;
about the next big scheduled marathon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.080
like the one the network ran over&nbsp;
Labor Day weekend. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:59.280
you could easily binge the past four seasons&nbsp;
on Peacock, but where's the challenge in that?

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:04.380
It's entirely possible that Taylor Sheridan could&nbsp;
end the Yellowstone saga with the fifth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.060
especially since he has a half-dozen other&nbsp;
Paramount projects in the making. It seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.660
unlikely, though, that the network would&nbsp;
want to fold on this modern western just yet.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:16.920
Many episodes throughout Season 4 felt&nbsp;
like backdoor pilots for other series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:21.960
which generated huge criticism, even from&nbsp;
longtime fans of the show. Jimmy's time down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:27.000
at the Four-Sixes Ranch in Texas was no doubt&nbsp;
a way to explore the world of 6666 long before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.500
the show's premiere. And the flashbacks&nbsp;
to the late 1800s Dutton family — led by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:36.120
Tim McGraw and Faith Hill — were an obvious&nbsp;
precursor to 1883. It seems that Sheridan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.900
is doing everything he can to expand his&nbsp;
Yellowstone empire before it loses steam.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:44.741
"You are the trailer park. I am the tornado."

00:08:44.741 --> 00:08:48.120
It's unclear where the story of the&nbsp;
Dutton family can still go. If they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.820
aren't going to give up their land to&nbsp;
developers, natives, or the government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.780
then who else is there left to fight?&nbsp;
And if Kayce and his family really are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:58.320
done with the Yellowstone for good, then&nbsp;
who is John Dutton actually fighting for?

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.060
If Yellowstone has taught us anything, it's&nbsp;
that one day it will all be gone — the Duttons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:07.080
their legacy, and possibly their open land.&nbsp;
Though we hope Yellowstone sticks around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.840
a while longer, everything&nbsp;
eventually comes to an end.

